  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This forty-five-minute audio capture documents the Mountain Goats performing twelve songs at Rough Trade East in London, United Kingdom, on Thursday, October 22, 2026 [1]. The recording was taped and transferred by Rairun, utilizing a CA-11 cards source connected to a Zoom F3 recorder to produce a FLAC file [1]. It is the only available recording of this specific performance, which serves as the four-hundred-and-sixty-seventh show in the archive's collection for the band [2]. The setlist features the track \"October, 2026,\" which is the only archived performance of that song [1][2]. Other selections include \"Last Day,\" \"Cry for Judas,\" and \"Song for Layne Staley,\" with the latter two identified as rare entries having five and six archived performances respectively [1][2]. The lineup continues with \"Andrew Eldritch Is Moving Back to Leeds,\" \"Cadaver Sniffing Dog,\" and \"Clemency for the Wizard King\" [1]. \"Crying on Eddie Nash's Grave\" is also a rare track with six archived performances, followed by \"You Were Cool\" [1][2]. The set concludes with \"Charlie Sheen Reaches Out to the Feds,\" \"Shallow Grave,\" and \"This Year\" [1][2]. This event follows a previous archived show from October 14, 2026, at TivoliVredenburg [2].",
